# bind FHS migration: named runtime /run/named -> /var/run/named.
#
# Stale-state policy (/var/run is persistent by design, never wiped):
# - PID file: cleared at (re)start in both inits (tracked-start
#   only, never against a live daemon); the daemon rewrites it.
#   Session keys and control state are recreated by named itself.
# - New /var/run/named: converged here on upgrade (named:named
#   0755, TSV-reserved base identity); created by tmpfiles.d
#   (systemd) and checkpath (OpenRC). The unit's old
#   RuntimeDirectory= could only create under /run, so tmpfiles.d
#   replaces it (rspamd precedent).
# - Old /run/named: volatile residue on tmpfs. Removed once empty;
#   left in place and reported while the old daemon runs.

dir /var/run/named 0755 named named
rmdir-if-empty /run/named
